        "title_top": "",
        "title": "Expert Backed Review Summary",
        "text": "<p>The TP-Link Archer GE650 is aimed squarely at gamers who want the performance benefits of Wi-Fi 7 along with gaming-focused network management. Its tri-band configuration provides rated speeds of up to <strong>5764 Mbps on 6 GHz, 4323 Mbps on 5 GHz, and 688 Mbps on 2.4 GHz</strong>, for a combined capacity of roughly 11 Gbps. A major advantage is its support for newer Wi-Fi 7 technologies. <strong>Multi-Link Operation (MLO)</strong> allows compatible devices to use multiple bands simultaneously, helping increase throughput, improve reliability, and reduce latency. The router also supports 320 MHz channels and 4K-QAM, making it better equipped for newer Wi-Fi 7 laptops, gaming PCs, and other compatible devices. Gaming features are another area where the GE650 stands apart from a standard home router. TP-Link's game acceleration system prioritizes gaming traffic across applications, devices, and game servers. There's also a dedicated gaming panel that provides real-time information about network status, router performance, accelerated devices and games, and RGB controls. Wired connectivity is equally capable. The router includes a <strong>5 Gbps WAN port, 5 Gbps LAN port, and three 2.5 Gbps LAN ports</strong>, giving users plenty of flexibility for multi-gig internet, gaming PCs, consoles, NAS devices, and other wired hardware. A USB 3.0 port is also included for additional connectivity. </p>",
        "body_align": "center",
        "content_width": "narrow",
        "align-heading": "center",
